<title>FRANCE: Fr Telecom sale needed for alliances - Fillon.</title>
<headline>Fr Telecom sale needed for alliances - Fillon.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French telecommunications minister Francois Fillon said on Wednesday that the partial privatisation of France Telecom was needed because of its alliance with Germany's Deutsche Telekom and Sprint Corp of the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;It is difficult to imagine that France Telecom would be the sole operator entirely in the hands of the state. That would be an unacceptable constraint and could rapidly endanger its international agreements, especially with Deutsche Telekom and Sprint,&quot; Fillon told business daily Les Echos.</p>
<p>The opposition Socialist party has vowed in its campaign in the current parliamentary election to stop the sale of France Telecom.</p>
</text>
